1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
In Burp Suite Enterprise Edition, you create sites to represent any websites or web applications that you want to scan.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
An onboarding wizard helps you to add your first site and then run a scan.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
We've provided a live, deliberately vulnerable website for you to scan so that you can follow along with this tutorial.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,000
The first step of the onboarding wizard prompts you to add your first site.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Start by giving it a name. This can be anything you like, but let's go with Portswigger Labs for this example.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,000
The site URL is the URL from which all scans of this site start.

7
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Any subpaths of the URL are included in the scope of the scan by default. Enter portswigger-labs.net.

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
This is a demo website with a few intentional vulnerabilities.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Using BebScanner may have unexpected effects on some applications.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Until you are fully familiar with its functionality and settings, you should only run scans against non-production systems.

11
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Do not run scans against third-party websites unless you have been authorised to do so by the owner.

12
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:12,000
For the scan configuration, you can choose from four preset modes that let you adjust the balance of speed and coverage.

13
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,000
For this scan, let's select Lightweight. The Lightweight mode completes in 15 minutes.

14
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Leave all of the options as their defaults and click Next. Create a scan.

15
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,000
You are now presented with various options for scheduling and configuring a scan of a site.

16
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Leave all of the options as their defaults and click Finish.

17
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:40,000
This schedules a one-off scan to run immediately.

18
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:46,000
To monitor the scan's progress, select Scans from the main navigation bar at the top of the screen.

19
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:52,000
You can then see your scan and some basic information about it, including the current status.

20
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:58,000
A minute or two after the scan begins running, colour-coded icons appear in the Issues column.

21
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:04,000
These indicate the number of security issues found by the scan for different severity levels.

22
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
You can click on the individual scan to view more detail.

23
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
On the Issues tab, you can monitor which issues are discovered in real-time.

24
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,000
We'll look closer at this tab in the next tutorial once the scan is finished.

25
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,000
This should only take about five minutes.

